{title: 603 - Christian, Seek Not Repose}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #603 • VIGILATE • 14.11}
{lyricist: Charlotte Elliott}
{composer: William H. Monk}
{key: Eb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 603}
{meta: tune VIGILATE}
{meta: meter 14.11}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Eb]Christian, [Ab/Eb]seek [Eb]not [Ab/Eb]yet repose, [Eb]Cast [Gm/D]thy [Cm]dreams [G7/B]of [Cm]ease [Ab]away;
[Eb]Thou aret [Ab/C]in [Eb/Bb]teh [Ab]midst [Bb7]of [Eb]foes; [Fm]Watch [Bb7]and [Eb]pray!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Eb]Gird thy heavenly [Ab/Eb]armor [Eb]on, Wear [Gm/D]it [Cm]ever, night [Ab]and [Bb]day;
[Eb]Ambushed [Ab/C]lies [Eb/Bb]the [Ab]evil [Eb]one; [Fm]Watch [Bb7]and [Eb]pray!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Eb]Hear the [Ab/Eb]victors who o'ercame; [Eb]Still [Gm/D]they [Cm]mark [G7/B]each [Cm]warrior's [Bb]way;
[Eb]All with [Ab/C]one [Eb/Bb]sweet [Ab]voice [Bb7]exclaim: [Fm]"Watch [Bb7]and [Eb]pray!"
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Eb]Hear, above all, [Ab/Eb]hear thy [Eb]Lord, Him [Gm/D]thou [Cm]lovest to [Ab]obey;
[Eb]Hide within thy [Ab]heart [Bb7]His [Eb]word; [Fm]"Watch [Bb7]and [Eb]pray!"
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[Eb]Watch, as [Ab/Eb]if [Eb]on [Ab/Eb]that alone [Eb]Hung [Gm/D]the [Cm]issue [G7/B]of [Cm]teh [Ab]day;
[Eb]Pray that [Ab/C]help [Eb/Bb]may [Ab]be [Bb7]send [Eb]down; [Fm]Watch [Bb7]and [Eb]pray!
{end_of_verse}
